package repl

// One goal-level rule shared by the routing prompt and tool schema. Selecting
// a convenient execution surface is not permission to drop a secondary goal.
const mixedTaskRouteContract = "Do not choose a route by the first or dominant subtask. A read-only measurement plus a requested source explanation is one analysis-pipeline task: use repo/hybrid, operation=investigate, source=mixed, current_source_evidence_mode=required; a requested source explanation remains required even when secondary. Shell commands used to collect its measurements are analysis tools, not a reason to select operation. The operation exception for repository facts applies to a concrete external deliverable or machine action, such as generating a slide deck from the repository, not to an answer combining a statistic and an implementation explanation. Mere working-directory access does not itself require source evidence; artifact-only analysis remains optional."

const operationGoalCompletionContract = "Evaluate every requested outcome, not only the successfully executed commands. Counts, directory listings and operation receipt metadata do not prove a requested explanation of repository implementation. A separate explanation needs inspected relevant source content and its actual relationships; naming files or describing this operation's own records is not that explanation. When this lane cannot satisfy an outstanding outcome, describe it in reason and emit partial_answer_possible rather than complete. Keep missing_inputs empty unless user-owned information is actually required; an unfinished source explanation is not a user-owned input to ask for. Never silently discard a secondary requirement."
